In 2016, almost 40% of people under 29 reported feeling proud to be an American.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.100
And then they hummed that lyric by Lee Greenwood.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.400
Checking back in 2023, that number is just 18%.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:33.500
So, okay, not really connecting on religion or patriotism, but hey, you can always meet people at your job.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.300
Ho-ho, never mind.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:39.100
The workplace has been completely upended in the last five years.

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:42.400
Just in time for Gen Z to enter the workforce and look for jobs.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.500
But maybe those jobs are remote jobs.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.300
Maybe they're in person.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.300
Maybe it's Halvesies.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.400
Maybe it's the gig economy.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.300
Maybe they'll strike.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:53.400
And all the while, there'll be a ton of inflation and Logan Paul is gonna be telling them they should be investing in crypto.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:59.200
70% of Millennials and Gen Z workers are considering quitting their jobs as I speak.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:05.000
And high percentages of Gen X workers in fields like tech and healthcare are feeling burned out due to work and finances.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:11.700
People's identities are no longer associated with the place they work because people don't view those places as reliable or helpful anymore.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.200
They feel financially insecure and underpaid.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:19.900
Enough so that basically half of all Zoomers, Millennials, and Gen Xers all have themselves a side hustle.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:24.000
My parents, by contrast, have worked in the same job for over 40 years.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.700
So for them, their job is a core part of their identity.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:31.400
But for young people now, they're disillusioned with corporate culture and mostly just want to get out.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.800
So, your job's not making you any positive connections these days.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.600
What then does that leave us with?

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:40.800
Well, according to identity theory, it leaves us with things like extreme political views.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.200
Or extreme viewpoints on topics like gender.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.000
Or extreme stances on race.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:51.400
All these areas where we've historically worked to break down barriers, improve communication, and at least attempt to work together.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:57.900
Instead, walls are now getting built back up as we attempt to define ourselves by how we're different from the other side.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.000
The scope of all of those things goes well beyond this little old theory on the internet.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:08.300
But suffice it to say, these are areas where a large percent of the population also feels divided, or isolated, or scared.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:11.500
And doesn't feel able to connect with those on the other side of the issue.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:19.700
So the TL;DR is that if you feel like it's a really lonely time out there, and it's bizarrely hard to make connections with your fellow humans on any basic level, you're right.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:22.900
We are more fractured and divided than ever everywhere we turn.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:27.900
And it's because the institutions around us that used to give us connection and identity are crumbling.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:29.500
So what then do we do?

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:34.600
In a time when we really want to feel connected with something, what's the thing that'll help make us feel connected?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:38.400
How do you possibly beat a series of systems that keep us siloed?

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.500
Well, ironically, it's in the place where we started this episode, stories.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:49.900
Whether that's in YouTube videos, movies, TV, video games, wherever, hearing other people's genuine stories about what they're going through makes us feel connected to them.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:53.800
It helps us understand that other people are going through what we're going through.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.200
It helps us to feel like we're not alone.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:57.900
They help us feel seen.

